     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**\n- **1700 mg total per day**, divided into doses, such as 850 mg twice daily\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note saying the dose was intentionally above the usual maximum. I'd expect pharmacy to question it."
      }
     ],
